   "tag": "p",
   "text": "archaeological artefact"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Wikimedia Commons · no author recorded by the source (opens in a new tab) Public domain"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Administrative dockets from Israel's northern capital."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "hebrew-inscribed ostraca found in Samaria, the capital of ancient Israel"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "CULTURE"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "archaeological artefact"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "RECORDED HOLDER"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Istanbul Archaeology Museums"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "ARCHAEOLOGY CATALOGUE · ROW BA-045 administrative corpus confirmed"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "What it supports. Harvard excavations recovered administrative Hebrew ostraca at Samaria in 1910."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "What it does not. The discoverer's early discussion is not a complete modern edition; the reign and clan identifications need individual texts and later scholarship."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Bears on: 1 Kings 16; Amos 6"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "text": "Matches a row of this project's archaeology catalogue"
  },
